# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore for admin_iconic_Visual_9594 workspace root
#
# Covers BOTH:
#   - Docs/                 (architecture docs, audit, c4 — tracked)
#   - PrototypeRacing/      (UE 5.6 project — Source/Config tracked, build + 24GB
#                            Content/ excluded)
#
# RULE: patterns have NO leading slash, so each matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth. This covers build dirs at the project root AND inside
# every Plugins/<Name>/ subdirectory in one shot.
#
# Decision 2C (this round): Blueprints / Content are NOT edited. The 24GB
# binary Content/ tree is intentionally NOT tracked. C++ (Source/), Config/,
# *.uproject, *.uplugin, plugin Source/ ARE tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- 24GB binary asset tree (project + plugin Content) -----------------------
# Blueprints (.uasset) live here. Not edited this round; do NOT track.
Content/

# --- Build-generated / cache directories (root + every Plugins/*/) -----------
Binaries/
Build/
Intermediate/
DerivedDataCache/
Saved/

# --- CodeGraph index store (the C++ knowledge graph DB) ----------------------
.codegraph/

# --- LikeC4 build output (generated static site; DSL source IS tracked) ------
# `likec4 build -o dist Docs/c4` emits the site to the WORKSPACE ROOT dist/,
# not Docs/c4/dist/. No leading slash → matches any dir named `dist` at any depth.
dist/
Docs/c4/node_modules/

# --- Astro Starlight portal (Docs/portal) ------------------------------------
# Source (src/, astro.config.mjs, package.json, copied likec4/ model) IS tracked.
# node_modules, build output and Astro cache are NOT tracked.
Docs/portal/node_modules/
Docs/portal/dist/
Docs/portal/.astro/
# Un-ignore portal content — the root-level Content/ rule (UE assets) would
# otherwise swallow Docs/portal/src/content/ via case-insensitive matching.
!Docs/portal/src/content/

# --- Structurizr (DSL + docs/ + adrs/ ARE tracked) ---------------------------
# CLI binaries (downloaded jar/zip) and generated static export are NOT tracked.
# workspace.dsl, docs/, adrs/ are source-of-truth and stay tracked.
Docs/structurizr/.tools/
Docs/structurizr/dist/

# --- IDE / tooling cruft -----------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sln
*.suo
*.opensdf
*.sdf
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace

# --- Compiled binaries / debug symbols ---------------------------------------
*.pdb
*.dll
*.exe
*.lib
*.exp
*.so
*.dylib

# --- OS junk -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~

# --- Misc local scratch ------------------------------------------------------
test.txt
